Revert the LocalSizeId emission floor from SPIR-V 1.2 back to SPIR-V 1.6.

Upstream commit eaff806e30cbe8ce138f1f3edcee5f0977a14a9a ("`local_size_*_id`
and SPIR-V 1.2", PR KhronosGroup/glslang#4052, merged 2026-08-24) lowered the
version gate that decides when glslang emits the LocalSizeId execution mode for
a spec-constant workgroup size, from EShTargetSpv_1_6 to EShTargetSpv_1_2.

That is invalid for the Vulkan environment.  OpExecutionModeId does exist since
SPIR-V 1.2, but the LocalSizeId *execution mode* additionally requires either
SPIR-V >= 1.6 or the maintenance4 feature, and glslang emits neither
SPV_KHR_maintenance4 nor the matching capability.  The resulting module is
rejected by spirv-val, which shaderc runs as part of `glslc -O`:

  shaderc: internal error: compilation succeeded but failed to optimize:
  LocalSizeId mode is not allowed by the current environment.
  This is allowed if you enable the maintenance4 feature (or use the
  --allow-localsizeid command line flag)

Upstream is aware the change produces unvalidatable output: the same commit adds
three entries to Test/baseResults/validation_fails.txt rather than fixing it.

This breaks every consumer that pairs `layout(local_size_x_id = N)` with
`--target-env=vulkan1.2` (SPIR-V 1.5) -- i.e. the whole ggml shader tree, so
sci-ml/{ggml,llama-cpp,ik_llama-cpp,koboldcpp,whisper-cpp,stable-diffusion-cpp}
with USE=vulkan.  Reported as obentoo/bentoo#42.  Raising the consumers to
vulkan1.3 would raise their hardware floor, and -O0 would cost shader
performance for everyone, so the fix belongs here: glslang is the component
producing an invalid module, the consumers are correct.

Only the version gate is reverted.  The rest of PR #4052 is deliberately kept:

  * the `local_size_*_id` below SPIR-V 1.2 diagnostic in
    glslang/MachineIndependent/ParseHelper.cpp -- untouched here, and still
    required by media-libs/mesa's mesa-astc-spirv1.2.patch;
  * the `&& needSizeId` guard newly applied to mesh/task shaders, which fixes
    KhronosGroup/glslang#3739 and makes this better than the released tag;
  * the redundant `needSizeId = true` cleanup.

Note for whoever reintroduces the test suite (this ebuild exposes no IUSE=test,
unlike ::gentoo): eaff806e also rewrote 12 files under Test/baseResults/, which
this revert does not touch, so those baselines will mismatch.

DROP THIS PATCH, do not rebase it, once upstream gates LocalSizeId correctly or
starts declaring SPV_KHR_maintenance4.  As of 2026-08-26 there is no upstream
fix and no upstream issue tracking it; commit 23076b376 (this snapshot's pin)
is main's HEAD.

